---
# swift-objc-wasm — Copyright 2026 Corey Earwood and the swift-objc-wasm contributors
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH Swift-exception
#
# NSObject's description and debugDescription are declared with Foundation's NSString. A module
# that loads a module named Foundation (swiftui-web's Foundation shadow) imports them as String,
# beside the String description that swiftui-web's WebFoundation gives every NSObject (it needs
# one where no Foundation is loaded), so `override var description` matched two and reading it
# was ambiguous. Swift sees the runtime's as __description and __debugDescription; the
# Objective-C selectors are unchanged.
#
# The runtime's header marks -performSelector: and its two withObject: forms as returning
# `id _Nullable`, so Swift saw `Unmanaged<AnyObject>?` and `perform(_:).takeUnretainedValue()`,
# as Apple's SDK lets it be written, did not compile. Apple's header leaves that return's
# nullability unspecified, so Swift sees `Unmanaged<AnyObject>!`; these notes say the same.
Name: ObjectiveC
Protocols:
- Name: NSObject
  Methods:
  - Selector: "performSelector:"
    MethodKind: Instance
    NullabilityOfRet: U
  - Selector: "performSelector:withObject:"
    MethodKind: Instance
    NullabilityOfRet: U
  - Selector: "performSelector:withObject:withObject:"
    MethodKind: Instance
    NullabilityOfRet: U
  Properties:
  - Name: description
    PropertyKind: Instance
    SwiftPrivate: true
  - Name: debugDescription
    PropertyKind: Instance
    SwiftPrivate: true
Classes:
- Name: NSObject
  Methods:
  - Selector: description
    MethodKind: Class
    SwiftPrivate: true
  - Selector: debugDescription
    MethodKind: Class
    SwiftPrivate: true
